  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 141 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nLow pressure deepens over the central Plains on Thursday, with a \nremnant baroclinic / frontal zone oriented NW to SE across the \nmidwest. Precip chances range from 20-70% across the CWA Thursday \n(highest towards the southwest corner of Wisconsin), with at least 1 \nminor shortwave providing some potential triggering for convection. \nThunderstorms would likely be weak if applicable, given the lack of \nreturn flow ahead of the low. The true warm sector appears to remain \nwell south into Illinois. \n\nPredominantly dry weather expected into Friday as high pressure \nbuilds into the Great Lakes region. As weak low pressure tracks \neastward across the midwest, showers and thunderstorms are looking \nlikely at times from Friday night through Saturday night, with \nlingering 20-30% chances into Sunday as the associated cold front \nswings through. Passing high pressure may then lead to predominantly \ndry weather into Monday. \n\nTemperatures should remain mild through the entire forecast period, \nlingering around seasonal norms or even slightly cooler.\n\nSheppard",
